[{"id":"VRCE-5-25-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":1,"english":"Being thus addressed angrily by Sītā, some of those Raksasis, beside themselves with ire, proceeded to relate this to the vicious-souled Ravana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.68,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"567ee64313cf901c570d4bdef5df908920c9a812f10d98a085240a213aa13828","compact":"64a31070032c7c61da6e6ce89a0a90fc53e8220160d1ee4cc4f58bbb37e857e8","nasal":"64a31070032c7c61da6e6ce89a0a90fc53e8220160d1ee4cc4f58bbb37e857e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":2,"english":"And approaching Sītā those grim-visaged demons again addressed her with words rude and rough.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff34554b054832e0b3c40b582d8f46cd30293ffa455e7625a61331f5021c7fbf","compact":"b2e887281e880fd56276f4eadceb2959fc2ccbf663d0c3cf5faf78a77d0aa982","nasal":"b2e887281e880fd56276f4eadceb2959fc2ccbf663d0c3cf5faf78a77d0aa982"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":3,"english":"O vile Sītă, O you bent on committing sin, we Rākşasīs shall today devour your flesh to the best of our satisfaction.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.94,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"539fd51dc4c838cb15468431e907975086c62e17d9ba025e4de80fbd82af9f92","compact":"6eb0ef8b2f13a0b3426c885347c522838bcd6133ce68f30c62afbc4f58f63b0a","nasal":"c23ae4334a8f2ea7c384140ef805cec47bc693c9846c65d5c1e7d8b0107d7f8f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":4,"english":"Beholding those vile demons threaten Sītā, a Raksasa matron, wise and old, named, Trijata cried.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.722,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e8be918fdf84af6fee979eaccac76b877c00fb03e012474a4782be8693fd46c9","compact":"951ab2c2492c0002ec1123aaf7817ad58c0ceccfbf7164418b541fda873b96f5","nasal":"951ab2c2492c0002ec1123aaf7817ad58c0ceccfbf7164418b541fda873b96f5"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":5,"english":"O vile demons, do youeat your own persons (The proper expression, I think, should be-“Eat me.” The commentator Rāmānuja explains Atmanam as your own bodies.) but do not devour Sītā, the daughter of Janaka and the esteemed daughter-in-law of the king Dasaratha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0fd972896601d4c0a3222f37fcbee6c1562a3a5d8c85bb9fea96776cdd6839a8","compact":"985c4279c54d27f9fec47797b5de941d6878288c4c9eda16eb51e5d9115328ea","nasal":"985c4279c54d27f9fec47797b5de941d6878288c4c9eda16eb51e5d9115328ea"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":6,"english":"I dreamt a terrible dream last night which made my down stand on their end. And in that dream I foresaw the overthrow of the Rāksasa race and the conquest of her husband.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"16a06f3eca24eb4350f207db8ea07ecb372d40601b69befbccf3396c83f7f47a","compact":"e25b2545632a5f2d28d81b95743490323c4a1702d408358349079db97dd03ae8","nasal":"e25b2545632a5f2d28d81b95743490323c4a1702d408358349079db97dd03ae8"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":7,"english":"And being thus addressed by Trijatā, those demons, exercised with wrath and terrified, accosted her with the following words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.917,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"593ef88182a5451675f1dfaed88567c031948229f67e5363fb25e6bf0d8c822d","compact":"3e5efa588e6f7f2e6ae42926dbebc967721799ceb3179145d72ed4d7dd116e23","nasal":"3e5efa588e6f7f2e6ae42926dbebc967721799ceb3179145d72ed4d7dd116e23"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":8,"english":"\"Do you relate (to us) what sort of dream didst you dream last night.\" And hearing those words proceeding from the mouths of the Rākşasīs, Trijatā began to describe the dream she had at the latter end of the night,","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.724,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fe28e5206bb17bc385c6e19714ff911a175750e7d48676c5d573003c2f4f16a9","compact":"da3ef4b80948ed62082433121ac92d3de4b669fbe47a15f7859e2f9834cc8563","nasal":"da3ef4b80948ed62082433121ac92d3de4b669fbe47a15f7859e2f9834cc8563"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":9,"english":"\"Do you relate (to us) what sort of dream didst you dream last night.\" And hearing those words proceeding from the mouths of the Rākşasīs, Trijatā began to describe the dream she had at the latter end of the night,","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6f83899a8f6a7e5f7d011e8b2708c53a99f182f5619db3d0978d8234b6ae0040","compact":"86b4a1e06b18d712b58ad6011e470d07e25288840311bba27594becfd98b425f","nasal":"86b4a1e06b18d712b58ad6011e470d07e25288840311bba27594becfd98b425f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":10,"english":"I saw Rāma, wearing garlands and clothed in white, ride in a celestial chariot, along with Lakşmaņa, made of ivory, traversing the etherial regions and drawn by a hundred steeds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"033222a01cb840f2feb5ea1bd226658edbebf7398fe96071d922c94f3d743731","compact":"216d0ffad5a93d5a2c826798bd83c56fc15cdfc4970d1c79e158a2ce33d2f6ba","nasal":"9b54566e934a85991fa2c0f4bde9faf865e977141b00d0ed16fa615667dea374"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":11,"english":"I saw in my dream to-night, that Sītā, clad in the purest white, appearing on a snow-white hill beaten by the waves of the ocean, had at last met Rāma, like to light joined to the Sun.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.929,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f21f6bd36a0db3e6189707c96a9aa1f32dc9d15be6b7ca669ffa5014b01a57c5","compact":"fdac55b692b90e765014d6a1141956c8dd355df8233cfdb9018917901b7b5545","nasal":"bc9d400aeee3a41fee985e0b86d0fa3c0da3831182945b5b10562906ccac71d1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":12,"english":"I again saw Rāma and Lakşmaņa appear in effulgence, seated on a huge elephant, having four tusks and resembling a bull.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.636,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"970a1a4e59be0fa6bab0d1c03385e99998c18638d4f1384697ad705281ec7355","compact":"1168b27e124cf28ef19a74b475c2a22efa5be8ec66f244c2ab44481634d0238a","nasal":"a6f77d6f6e6f8d4a57ae2bb272192588927662f12ec239bd8c7a635efe923beb"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":13,"english":"Thereupon those two (brothers), resplendent like to the Sun by their own effulgence, and wearing white garlands and clothes, appeared near Janaka's daughter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.629,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"99fe2af485238a31f7df5872e8334ba005d4093eec3ef3ed58a8a9b8b19be4cc","compact":"b1dbd297f0333fee0d6c4c89c67fa678a96860b2d89deb3e164f036a05edfdef","nasal":"f328a77c79d0eb1c2a7fefa7f7b11d19b9f362da2a9ddb711b8854aa6429bfd5"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":14,"english":"And the lotus-eyed Jānakī, on the top of the hill situate on the welkin, first fell on the lap of her husband and then stationed herself on the neck of the elephant guided by her husband. Then I saw Sītā rubbing the Sun and the Moon with her two hands.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.677,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a037518353236341872cf76ab14ffea5abbcdc4bbf909cfbad3b15d48eb7acab","compact":"9a4fd2fed9c73e2c31dc80f5023f640dc2a94aa6491dc5578093cd8871acbdf0","nasal":"8bb339bc667e55ef8ffb052822652370c51d9303e551e0e767ef93a8cef19e3c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":15,"english":"And the lotus-eyed Jānakī, on the top of the hill situate on the welkin, first fell on the lap of her husband and then stationed herself on the neck of the elephant guided by her husband. Then I saw Sītā rubbing the Sun and the Moon with her two hands.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5405b854fd5feef9929a39699136558520d88e552efc00e24a462ce40ddacf1f","compact":"64d01f9ac85793dd2e106e947e279e2dffdff19ccfbc8561813ba67d1eccda64","nasal":"dad52198b93cdf5995e109879b41f65e661dd02717d5ee27d9283f5ea34f1b78"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":16,"english":"Then that best of the elephants, with those two princes and the large eyed Sītā on him, stood high above Lanka. I again saw Rāma, clad in white, and adorned with garlands, ride along with Lakşmaņa in a chariot drawn by eight white bullocks.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.97,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7d79dc6279c671fe7e7de95fc239e30f7b367c41a7b1ca27ba0d810e1e33ce4b","compact":"4a1494f4382c892ab0156139ecddf8343c22c5816bae8243d4475d4ecafbc804","nasal":"fa519080abc0aa8a03f61ce72508724583cb6e9cbf0ad5ddb1899c3d45dde843"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-17","kanda":5,