t an auspicious sign.)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.381,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"25f980fcdb8421e5e1c0e43b9b3608a2c502de8d7d7da14eb9aae2fd0eca2255","compact":"c187dd760c23742706fcc14fd268bb0fe8ce87ffbab080cb8be1811fb0fa94dd","nasal":"c187dd760c23742706fcc14fd268bb0fe8ce87ffbab080cb8be1811fb0fa94dd"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":20,"english":"And a dark woman, clad in a crimson cloth, and bedaubed with mud, dragged the Ten-necked demon, entwining herself around his neck. Then followed the mighty Kumbhakarņa (Rāvana's brother) and all the sons of Rāvana, shaved and shorn and besmeared with oil. And they all proceeded southward—the Ten-necked demon on a boar, Indrajit (Rāvana's son-the name signifies the conqueror of the lord of the celestials) on a porpoise, and Kumbhakarņa on a camel.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d9e9ff31ed6efdcbfbf27f50bb97e5535872ea39c337b78cafcdb8ebb7a6409a","compact":"2c5bef40ea31de0b78ee89c1d7d7f89e81c07eb87e6dd2f3d509f7daba43069a","nasal":"74ff6c35a18d9c12c63bc390daa0352638971ac461963a02660057951c602fe6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":21,"english":"And a dark woman, clad in a crimson cloth, and bedaubed with mud, dragged the Ten-necked demon, entwining herself around his neck. Then followed the mighty Kumbhakarņa (Rāvana's brother) and all the sons of Rāvana, shaved and shorn and besmeared with oil. And they all proceeded southward—the Ten-necked demon on a boar, Indrajit (Rāvana's son-the name signifies the conqueror of the lord of the celestials) on a porpoise, and Kumbhakarņa on a camel.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.897,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"285df1eb20b895bef0f26fe7a1134f7456a8564fffb70789764491b30fe2c27e","compact":"080308a56ddfaaf61210651cbbb86b221491462db519ab0baab6fdc1b4d12481","nasal":"88ba191bd0409fd7e85ca91a83ec2f9367facd22e0a1c152cc98049bc11859a6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-22","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":22,"english":"And there was audible in the large assembly sound of music and stringed instruments. And all the Rākşasa wearing crimson clothes and garlands, were quaffing oil, I saw the royal and picturesque city Lankā with her steeds, cars and elephants, drowned in the ocean, having her gateways and ornamented arches broken.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025022","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4c5dd9434070ab5db1bf4688788e0c7908748d5b7d198f7e235b92c8ecae1c23","compact":"77d7e3021ae1359a378bc322fecc059d6189713071450ce9483e5c7342b84d87","nasal":"77d7e3021ae1359a378bc322fecc059d6189713071450ce9483e5c7342b84d87"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-23","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":23,"english":"And there was audible in the large assembly sound of music and stringed instruments. And all the Rākşasa wearing crimson clothes and garlands, were quaffing oil, I saw the royal and picturesque city Lankā with her steeds, cars and elephants, drowned in the ocean, having her gateways and ornamented arches broken.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025023","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4b5d8333856fb2d830cbed1c1abc5943502099d71878fd60624491ea0c3ccb07","compact":"ffb4c05a5c13c5ccb8879f03ace37542ccff4c4738922e00ed14c586b9901248","nasal":"8c6278e7f8616697251039e6e776ee2c66a1015558ae16810eabb045a2593bb4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-24","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":24,"english":"And in Lanka, covered with dust, Raksasa women laughing and making terrible sound, were engaged in quaffing oil.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025024","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"01546525920c6fc2ce0ac36bf3ce4530477a405a27e4f6c10a8d1684126cc74b","compact":"9a2cfdd4865e64adf8b028e656dcf4b359b7e34db2dac244c678638c2df0c420","nasal":"8b1ebfcf19dac43b6b3d7ad11196120a066ebb77c89b4e40a25b4bceea79e0fb"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-25","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":25,"english":"I saw all the leading Raksasas-Kumbhakarņā and others, dark-hued and wearing crimson clothes, emerged in an abyss of cow dung.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025025","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"db73ee50288d364c78b707f1c432850c9680ffe66a2381fc78980df1a6ef7855","compact":"d637168829e347426f18005d2bd4cc0136e33a5aae61875e7b0594016f9ac91e","nasal":"72159669e7721ee8bd760be222db8af17656f690f672a97877f3847398b18611"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-26","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":26,"english":"Do youtherefore fly at some distance, and will find that Rāghava shall regain Sītā. And exercised with ire he shall destroy you all along with the Raksasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025026","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"663f07798ec730a9861e96cec65a4e68f9c326acf0f828ec8db54c0fbe5b813c","compact":"bdfb3620b2ecb7744c21c6433dec060c7dc2812b2aa4f8688c1d65627a526ba4","nasal":"bdfb3620b2ecb7744c21c6433dec060c7dc2812b2aa4f8688c1d65627a526ba4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-27","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":27,"english":"Rāghava shall never brook, his esteemed and beloved spouse, living in the forest, being taunted and threatened by you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.761,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025027","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"905d6afdf055eef6ca96a32af18db9c947196cab81515753b59859a321609383","compact":"45c9462096270ae7868c934e1ff238188fbe8751514a50a9fb0848b89269805e","nasal":"44195175345724c4590c591b96a642269a8c02bcf215ece4404fc06828d62162"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-28","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":28,"english":"No more with rough words therefore; do you console the lady and humbly pray her to forgive you. This I think proper.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.817,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025028","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"df894c8586a796cdebfdcc5d204b2bb966fda862342d48c2d2d47eda0b9bae60","compact":"4684fbbf1dc3122c6afc749ef8c13f5af9c9e9ae82e6bd345ba863fef15db4ff","nasal":"7fac6b1616d5c50ac7f06cf3a1e42cc209f9ddd2c754d32c0a0bd81abb02ee51"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-29","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":29,"english":"Surely shall she, divested of misfortune, he reconciled to her beloved and excellent husband, regarding whom, in her misery, I have dreamt such a dream.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025029","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"40318381b6951e85767d726d40689ecbfef874c82d76db00b51a5aab20d56eb2","compact":"8dcbb86b24a4595b589ab89842867c9d1ea3830512eddd48540667453444b851","nasal":"8dcbb86b24a4595b589ab89842867c9d1ea3830512eddd48540667453444b851"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-30","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":30,"english":"YouRaksasis! You have threatened her, do youimplore her forgiveness—no more with harsh words. Forsooth, from Rāghava shall proceed the mighty disaster of the Rākṣasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.91,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025030","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8b9943d2ee1a29a41a1dc456e4befff4649b6150b09240655ca7afe1b46d065c","compact":"62f7b63afc4809f79a0b641bbc07bfe05c3438b78b62b1f9146860bcf7628696","nasal":"62f7b63afc4809f79a0b641bbc07bfe05c3438b78b62b1f9146860bcf7628696"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-31","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":31,"english":"If Maithili, the daughter of the king Janaka, be pleased with you (for your imploring her forgiveness) you might be saved from the mighty disaster.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025031","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ebd29e8a33db2ac42239d18eabcc4e0ef6372a4103ef5af8ff3f26f520b0a6f7","compact":"cb4ffa4e4d85d84d99b640cf6f4d41d5e8df6e9b845a8bb1611eb7e34edb90d0","nasal":"099516da305a67070ef5c7de164ee48d92cf9266262cc920e673ae869211ef3a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-32","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":32,"english":"I do not perceive any inauspicious mark on the person of this large-eyed dame. It appears from the paleness of her countenance that she has been overcome by misfortune.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.765,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025032","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1df5979b160208206d5a6f2d080f74c068c8a54bddc2fb7e2eb8f5fc157ece6a","compact":"10cda687626ad9aad42fd181af92a47a1aa79a2e992c435ea5e992e32667f930","nasal":"dcc170afaf101ed25f2de702a9e1e53f52951eae5cbd422fd999e8d4b5cace48"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-33","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":33,"english":"And I saw in my dreams) this worshipful damsel, unworthy of any misfortune, stationed in the welkin.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.853,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025033","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9fe587bd5e5a097a2f38403b72cc3dce0e2ada9b18a4ca5d69776f3c290c6726","compact":"cdedcb0e3b284752ff08a4ebd6c7f07919fc0ca898801446e2c8b4212e5928b4","nasal":"7f3f6e4d0bfd51420d2ff4ddf01236fa863788c7cf26f4044e5e5d9defe0a262"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-25-34","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":25,"verse":34,"english":"Verily I do perceive, before me, the satisfaction of Vaidehi's end, the destruction of the lord of the Rākşasas and the conquest of Raghava.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-27-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5025034","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9247f6344a359677cac1983da3e853d4b08047c8a045e4879fcdba28414cfeaa","compact":"f5d